Compile libgcc without the C library. It does not need one, and must not see the
SDK's headers: their LONG_MIN is (-2147483648), which is unsigned in C89, and that
turns the range check in __fixunsdfsi around, so a conversion of a double to a long
long comes out wrong or never finishes. It also means that nothing of the SDK goes
into building the compiler.

--- a/gcc/config/mips/t-ecoff
+++ b/gcc/config/mips/t-ecoff
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
 
 # We must build libgcc2.a with -G 0, in case the user wants to link
 # without the $gp register.
-TARGET_LIBGCC2_CFLAGS = -G 0
+TARGET_LIBGCC2_CFLAGS = -G 0 -Dinhibit_libc
 
 # fp-bit and dp-bit are really part of libgcc1, but this will cause
 # them to be built correctly, so... [taken from t-sparclite]
